 ## Background
-LU-NeRF was introduced in 2023 [S2]. It addresses the challenges of few-shot novel view synthesis and optimizing unknown poses in a combined setting [S1]. The method builds on the idea of breaking up a large scene into mini-scenes to overcome the non-convexity of global pose optimization without accurate initialization [S1]. It is related to methods like BARF, which also optimizes camera poses but requires coarse initialization and uses positional encoding [S1].
